{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Vandermonde","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Central","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.NatAntidiagonal","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.bracket_sum_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.bracket_sum_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BinomialSquareSums.lean#L150-L217","doc":"**The step-5 collapse.** With `m = r + 1`, the hook-shape bracket sum collapses:\n\n`Σ_{k ≤ m} C(m,k)²·(3k² − 3mk + m(m−1)) = (m−1)(m−2)·C(2m−2, m−1)`.\n\nStated over `ℤ` at `m = r + 1` (so the subtractions are genuine): the left side is the bracket\nsum, the right side `r(r−1)·C(2r, r)`. The factor `(r − 1) = (m − 2) = (n − 3)` is the exact\nsource of the `n = 3` zero of `ν_n`.\n\nProof: substitute the three moments (`sum_sq_mul_choose_sq`, `two_mul_sum_mul_choose_sq`,\n`sum_choose_sq`), eliminate `C(2r+2, r+1)` via `succ_mul_central_succ`, and collapse the\npolynomial coefficient `6(r+1)² − 2(2r+1)(r+3) = 2r(r−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.succ_mul_central_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.succ_mul_central_succ","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BinomialSquareSums.lean#L143-L148","doc":"**Central-binomial step**: `(m+1)·C(2m+2, m+1) = 2(2m+1)·C(2m, m)` — the ratio of successive\ncentral binomial coefficients, in division-free form (`Nat.succ_mul_centralBinom_succ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.two_mul_sum_cube_mul_choose_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.two_mul_sum_cube_mul_choose_sq","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BinomialSquareSums.lean#L112-L139","doc":"**Third moment (division-free)**: `2·Σ_{k ≤ m+1} k³·C(m+1, k)² = (m+1)²(m+2)·C(2m, m)`.\nAbsorption reduces the cube to `(k+1)·[(m+1)·C(m,k)]²`, then the first and zeroth moments at\norder `m` finish. Recorded for completeness of the moment family: the cubic terms **cancel** in\nthe hook-shape bracket (see `bracket_sum_collapse`), so this moment is not consumed there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.sum_sq_mul_choose_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.sum_sq_mul_choose_sq","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BinomialSquareSums.lean#L97-L110","doc":"**Second moment**: `Σ_{k ≤ m+1} k²·C(m+1, k)² = (m+1)²·C(2m, m)`. The `k = 0` term vanishes;\nabsorption turns each remaining term into `(m+1)²·C(m, k−1)²`, and the zeroth moment finishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.succ_mul_choose_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.succ_mul_choose_succ","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BinomialSquareSums.lean#L91-L95","doc":"**Absorption**: `(k+1)·C(m+1, k+1) = (m+1)·C(m, k)` — the standard index-shift that turns a\n`k`-weighted binomial into an unweighted one at one lower order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.two_mul_sum_mul_choose_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.two_mul_sum_mul_choose_sq","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BinomialSquareSums.lean#L66-L87","doc":"**First moment (division-free)**: `2·Σ_{k ≤ m} k·C(m,k)² = m·C(2m, m)`. Reflecting\n`k ↦ m − k` leaves the weight invariant, so summing the two orderings replaces `k` by\n`k + (m − k) = m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.sum_choose_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums.sum_choose_sq","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BinomialSquareSums.lean#L56-L62","doc":"**Vandermonde square sum**: `Σ_{k ≤ m} C(m,k)² = C(2m, m)`. The central Vandermonde\nconvolution `C(m+m, m) = Σ_{i+j=m} C(m,i)·C(m,j)` with the symmetry `C(m, m−k) = C(m, k)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}